* Grover's algorithm
** The problem
*** N candidates, M solutions
*** Only an oracle to test one
*** No structure to exploit
** One iteration
*** Oracle flips the phase
*** Diffusion D = WRW
*** Inversion about the average
*** Rotation by 2θ
** Iteration count
*** sin²θ = M/N
*** About (π/4)√(N/M)
*** Too many iterations undo the work
*** Unknown M: random counts (BBHT)
left side
** Limits
*** Ω(√N) lower bound (BBBV)
*** Exactly optimal (Zalka)
*** √S gain from S machines
*** Generalised by amplitude amplification
** Cryptography
*** Key search: 2^(k/2) iterations
*** Hash preimages: same bound
*** Reversible oracle, error correction
*** NIST: 2^170 / MAXDEPTH for AES-128
*** Public keys fall to Shor, not Grover
